    "result_text": "There's only the one test class (`AcceptanceTest`), and the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required the owner response to expose `membershipTier`: `SILVER` when `namesakeCount` is 0 and an email is present, otherwise `BRONZE`.\n\nSince this is a derived, read-only response field (like the existing `displayName`, `initials`, and `membershipNumber`), I implemented it the same way the project handles those:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `membershipTier` property (enum `SILVER`/`BRONZE`, `readOnly`) to the `Owner` schema, so the OpenAPI generator emits the field and its `OwnerDto.MembershipTierEnum` on the generated DTO.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression computing the tier from the entity:\n   ```\n   SILVER  when namesakeCount != null && namesakeCount == 0 && email is non-blank\n   BRONZE  otherwise\n   ```\n\nThe existing `namesakeCount` pipeline (`AssignOwnerNamesakeCount`) already populates the entity before save, and both the create response (`RespondWithOwnerCreated`) and `GET /api/owners/{id}` (`RespondWithOwner`) go through `toOwnerDto`, so the field is consistent on read-back \u2014 which is what the tests assert.\n\nResults: the two new acceptance tests (`coreSilverWhenUniqueWithEmail`, `functionalityBronzeWhenNoEmail`) pass, and the full suite reports **BUILD SUCCESS** (2 tests, 0 failures).",
